rdimensional computing: An introduction to computing in distributed representation with high-dimensional random vectors","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b23","section_path_id":"2.2","quote":"(Kanerva, 2009)","offset":1613}]},{"raw_text":"The algebraic mind: Integrating connectionism and cognitive science\n\t\t\n\t\t\tGFMarcus\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2003\n\t\t\tMIT press","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b24","section_path_id":"2.1","quote":"(Marcus, 2003)","offset":2404}]},{"raw_text":"The magical number seven, plus or minus two: some limits on our capacity for processing information\n\t\t\n\t\t\tGAMiller\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tPsychological review\n\t\t\n\t\t\t63\n\t\t\t2\n\t\t\t81\n\t\t\t1956","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"The magical number seven, plus or minus two: some limits on our capacity for processing information","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b25","section_path_id":"2.1","quote":"(Miller, 1956)","offset":487}]},{"raw_text":"The cognitive revolution: a historical perspective\n\t\t\n\t\t\tGAMiller\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tTrends in cognitive sciences\n\t\t\n\t\t\t7\n\t\t\t3\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t2003","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":"The cognitive revolution: a historical perspective","anchors":[{"ref_id":"b26","section_path_id":"2.2","quote":"(Miller, 2003)","offset":188}]},{"raw_text":"Computation: finite and infinite machines\n\t\t\n\t\t\tMLMinsky\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t1967\n\t\t\tPrentice-Hall, Inc","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b27","section_path_id":"1","quote":"(Minsky, 1967)","offset":2198}]},{"raw_text":"Machine learning: a probabilistic perspective\n\t\t\n\t\t\tKPMurphy\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2012\n\t\t\tMIT press","doi":null,"arxiv_id":null,"title":null,"anchors":[{"ref_id":"b28","section_path_id":"4.4","quote":"(Murphy, 2012)","offset":1866}]},{"raw_text":"Holographic Reduced Representation: Distributed representation for cognitive structures\n\t\t\n\t\t\tTAPlate\n\t\t\n\t\t\n\t\t\t2003\n\t\t\tCSLI","doi":null,"arxiv_id":